BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mausritter RPG
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T150000
UID:6a2c2ec816554cd59fc85d80@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You are mere mice in an enormous world full of dangers: cats\
 , snakes\, and venomous spiders to name but a few! Fortunately you have we
 apons (of sorts): a fishhook fitted onto a twig\, a sewing needle or mayb
 e just a sharp stone lashed to a twig with some old tooth floss. You have
  allies as well\, and hopefully between you\, you also have a plan. Will t
 his be enough to defeat your enemies\, plunder their treasure and earn eve
 rlasting fame and glory? Much will depend on the plan\, and a little will
  depend on the dice!\nMausritter\nis a swords and whiskers role-playing ga
 me set in the vein of classic stories such as\nMouse Guard\nand\nRedwall\n
 . The stakes are high\,\,with perilous combat\, sneaky plans\, treasure an
 d a slim chance to become the heroes of your colony. Some mice may lose th
 eir lives (heroically of course)\, but you can just create a new mouse and
  play on!\nRegistration opens June 27th and is the best way to guarantee 
 a spot.\nAges 8-12 strongly recommended.\nInformation Collection Notice:\n
 The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public L
 ibrary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d)
 . The information will only be used for event and program registration\, d
 elivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your infor
 mation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-3
 97-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Rooms A & B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2c2ec816554cd59fc85d80
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
