BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature's Enduring Gifts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T113000
UID:6a5e3558daaaf4f51a2056cc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Emancipation Month with a musical and interactive p
 resentation!\nHosted by Frances Greenidge\, this is an organic retelling o
 f the impact of the American Folksong\, Follow the Drinking Gourd. This fo
 lksong was used by fugitive slaves in the mid-1800’s to remember and use
  the clues in nature to escape towards freedom in Canada by following the 
 Underground Railroad.\nThis educational and dynamic performance program te
 aches participants about the natural signs and elements that guided enslav
 ed people on their journey to freedom via the Underground Railroad.\nDrop-
 in! All are welcome.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e3558daaaf4f51a2056cc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Club de lecture de bande dessinée
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T170000
UID:69e2a4b4bd5c392c7644e236@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:*English text follows*\nPratiquez votre français pendant les 
 vancances d'été ! Chaque mois\, lisez une nouvelle bande dessinée en f
 rançais de votre choix en lien avec le thème proposé\, et venez nous e
 n parler. Bien sûr\, nous nous amuserons aussi avec diverses activités.\
 nLe thème du mois de juillet est\nl'eau\n. Choisissez un livre parmi ceux
  mentionnés ci-dessous ou\ntout autre ouvrage correspondant au thème\n.\
 nLa rivière de mon grand-père\nde Rémi Farnos\nLes océans\nde Hubert R
 eeves\, David Vandermuelen et Daniel Cassanave\nLe mystère du lac\nde Jas
 on Pamment\nPour enfants âgés de 8 à 12 ans.\nPractice your French duri
 ng the Summer break! Each month\, read a new comic book or graphic novel i
 n French of your choice related to the selected theme\, and come talk abou
 t it. Of course\, the discussion will be followed up with various fun acti
 vities.\nThe theme for the month of August is\nwater\n. Choose a book amon
 g those listed below or\nany other that corresponds to the theme.\nLa rivi
 ère de mon grand-père\nby Rémi Farnos\nLes océans\nby Hubert Reeves\
 , David Vandermuelen and Daniel Cassanave\nLe mystère du lac\nby Jason Pa
 mment\nFor kids aged 8 to 12.\nAccessibilité:\nLe sous-titrage en direct 
 ou automatique\, l’interprétation en langue des signes\, les services d
 ’intervenant\, ou les services d’accompagnement sont disponibles sur d
 emande. Veuillez soumettre votre demande au moins deux semaines à l’av
 ance à :\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e2a4b4bd5c392c7644e236
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
