SUMMARY:Digital Creators Camp: Design\, Film\, Tech & Streaming
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T110000
UID:6a395b889571053ed63bf1a4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all future YouTubers\, filmmakers\, inventors\, and di
 gital creators!\nReady to turn your big ideas into awesome digital project
 s? Join us for an action-packed\, 4-day workshop where you’ll learn how 
 to design graphics\, edit movies\, play with tech hardware\, and produce y
 our own live stream.\nWhether you want to make videos\, design cool graphi
 cs\, or learn how the tech behind your favorite creators works\, this hand
 s-on camp has something for you.\nWhat We're Learning\nDay 1: Canva\n– K
 ick things off by learning graphic design secrets to create stunning visua
 ls and digital art.\nDay 2: iMovie\n– Step behind the camera and master 
 the basics of video editing\, sound effects\, and cinematic storytelling.\
 nDay 3: Arduino\n– Code meets the real world! Get hands-on with hardware
 \, circuits\, and microcontrollers to see how tech is built.\nDay 4: OBS S
 tudio\n– Put it all together and learn how the pros broadcast\, manage m
 ulti-screen layouts\, and set up a live streaming studio.\nThe Details:\nW
 ho:\nCreative kids ages\n8 to 12\nWhen:\nMonday through Thursday\,\n10:00 
 AM – 11:00 AM\nWhere:\n[Agincourt Library/Learning Centre]\n⚠️\nImpo
 rtant Note:\nThis is a sequential\, cumulative program. Because each day b
 uilds directly on the last\,\nregistrants must attend all 4 sessions\nto p
 articipate.\nSpace is limited and spots will fill up fast.  Registration
  opens up two weeks prior to the camp start day on July 13th at 9:00 a.m.\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M
 4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a395b889571053ed63bf1a4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
