BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Anne of the Library-on-the-Hill Story and Craft
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260811T150000
UID:69c59f1581b67dfe32af3a99@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:'Growing up in the shadow of the Great War\, Anne finds comfor
 t in her neighbourhood library\, where she loses herself in books\, often 
 imagining herself as part of the story. She particularly loves the books o
 f LM Montgomery — and her imagination really takes off when she learns h
 er beloved author is in town.'\n"Anne of the Library-On-The-Hill" (Plumlea
 f Press\, August 2024)\, presented by the book's author Catherine Little\,
  celebrates iconic Canadian author\, Lucy Maud Montgomery\, and her connec
 tion to Toronto.  It is an homage to L.M. Montgomery\, libraries and imagi
 nation. After the story children will make a simple craft.\nPlease note: t
 his program is for children with adult accompaniment. This program is suit
 able for children 6 years old and above. This program has registration for
  up to 25 children.\nWhen signing up please only indicate the number of ch
 ildren attending.
LOCATION:Gerrard/Ashdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c59f1581b67dfe32af3a99
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
