BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mermaid Paint Pallet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T150000
UID:6a3bfe8bc52cdc3600ec848b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Part 1: We’ll be making paint pallets (can also be used as 
 jewlery dish or for display) using air dry clay\, seashells and assorted M
 ermaid themed bits and bobs!\nPart 2: We’ll be painting the air dried p
 allets with iridecent shimmery paint to seal/waterproof our mermaid themed
  paint pallets! Please only come to this day if you’ve attended Part 1\,
  as we’ll only be painting our pallets during this session.\n**\nRegist
 ration required for both sessions\n**Parents/caregivers\, please only make
  a registration for the child attending
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3bfe8bc52cdc3600ec848b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around  the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T173000
UID:69e8d4e68ddc1caf5f1e827d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The North York Central Library and its neighbourhood is home t
 o a variety of trees. Join the\nCity of Toronto Urban Forestry\nstaff to e
 xplore the natural world on a local neighbourhood walk. Learn how to recog
 nize different species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological i
 mportance.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\n
 Please note\, the tour will start and end at the North York Central Librar
 y\, Room 1\, and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staf
 f. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress an
 d prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. hats\, sunscreen\, wa
 ter\, comfortable shoes).\nRegistration is required.\nThis program takes p
 lace rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, you will be
  notified of an alternative date.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e8d4e68ddc1caf5f1e827d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet and Create with Mireille Messier
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T140000
UID:6a0dcf9a0c0f2c4503fabb9d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Gnomes and hedgehogs and magic\, oh my!\nJoin bilingual author
  Mireille Messier as she read her award-winning picture book The Magic Cap
 .\nThen\, create your own take-home 'Hedgehog With a Magic Cap' craft!\nTh
 e Magic Cap
LOCATION:Daniel G. Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0dcf9a0c0f2c4503fabb9d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to 3D Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260825T193000
UID:6a50ecce0d65ac36003ebcb2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how 3D printers work and how you can print at the Toront
 o Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs.\nIn this lecture\, we will c
 over:\n•Basics of 3D Printing\n•How to prepare a 3D design file for pr
 inting on a Prusa 3D printer using PrusaSlicer\n•How to access and use 3
 D printers at the Digital Innovation Hubs at the Toronto Public Library\n
 •Best practice for 3D printing and where to find designs\n•Review of t
 he rules and guidelines for using 3D printers at the Toronto Public Librar
 y\nNote: Customers are no longer required to attend a mandatory 3D printin
 g class prior to using a 3D printer at the Toronto Public Library’s Digi
 tal Innovation Hubs. This class is for those who are interested in learnin
 g more about 3D printing and how to use the Prusa software.\nRegistration 
 is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Hub\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a50ecce0d65ac36003ebcb2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wonder Workshop: Out of this World Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T150000
UID:6a0e3ad7fab4ff0f649a8866@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever imagined what it would be like to travel to oute
 r space? Join us to learn about space and the red planet then design your 
 own spacecraft. Brainstorm creative ways to solve problems you might face 
 on your journey. Plus\, enter a prize draw for a chance to win an awesome 
 book. For kids ages 6-10. Space is limited.\nInformation Collection Notice
